// Unless sound is off (0x80043626), sets the music's volume (the handle start_music keeps at 0x80043620; stop_music stops it) to `volume` held to 0..0x100 (0 or less resets the stored level 0x80043624 to 0x100 and uses 0), only when it changed from 0x80043624 (set_sound_volume). Callers func_80017C64 (a song played), run_pause_menu. (2026-11-12, names2: renamed from set_main_sound_volume -- 0x80043620 is the music's handle, as start_music and stop_music show.)
// From the N64 function at 0x800039BC (31 instructions).
// Called by: play_music_song, run_pause_menu, play_song_mod_copy.
// Random-tested: 200000 plain random inputs, all instructions reached, no difference. In play: 59 comparisons, no difference (caller twin v11, 0.84, match_tag, menu_from_attract, modes_reg_rumble (match not reached), modes_regular_boot, rules_single_hardcore, select_wcw, smoke_singles; see the header's caller-twin note).
