// Makes (or finds) the text texture for `text` in `style` and returns its record (find_text_texture_entry; NULL when the table is full or the picture can't be had): text with bit 30 set is a number (format_number into a buffer); style bits 4-5 an outline (margin 0x80069664 = 8 for 0x10, 2 for 0x20, 1 for 0x30, else 0); measures it (measure_text_texture, which sets +0xC / +0xE / +0x10 and the size +8), gives it heap memory (heap_alloc) unless the running total 0x80045978 would pass 0x7FFF, clears it, draws it (draw_text_into_texture), slants it with style bit 3 (slant_text_texture_lines) and outlines it (outline_text_texture, through a work copy). Callers set_name_box_superstar, cached_text_picture.
