// Plays the sound for cue `cue` (the s16 table 0x80048238[cue]): sound 0x46 goes round three handles (0x80076558 + 4 x *0x800484F4) at most every 20 frames (*0x800484E8); others start unless their handle (0x80076280 + 4 x sound) is still playing; the volume by the area like keep_ambient_sound_playing (*0x800A8968: under 20 0x80, 20 0x70, more 0x50). `cue` 0 or less only keeps the ambient loop going (keep_ambient_sound_playing). Callers play_wrestler_sound, reset_entrance_sequence and the scene / entrance code. Reading (from the ambient loop it goes with): the crowd's reactions. (2026-11-12, names3: confirmed from the lifted C++: volume 0x80 / 0x70 / 0x50 by *0x800A8968 against 20; sound 0x46 only while *0x800484E8 < 0 (then 20), play_sound(0x46, 0x80, 0x80, 0, -1) into handle (n + 1) % 3, set_sound_volume.)
