// Loads the menus' picture `text` (a picture or text number, through menu_text_picture_data) as the texture to draw with: adds to the display list at *`display_list` load_ci_texture_block's commands for its palette and its whole width (+4) x height (+6) of pixels, 8 bits each when its +8 is 8, else 4. Returns the picture's record (width +4, height +6), or 0 when there is none (then nothing is added). It draws nothing itself: the callers add the rectangle or vertices after it (e.g. draw_results_backdrop loads picture 0x65 and then writes its quad's corners). load_menu_picture_texture is the same with wrap settings. 32 callers. (2026-11-12: renamed from draw_menu_text, which the code doesn't do.)
