// The match camera's shot for two men in the ring (update_match_camera; mod/src/arena_ringstage.c: 'the ring's two men go to func_800E38A4'): from the pair `pair` (two slots, u16) and their places (0x8017C870, 0x14 apart) takes the larger of their gaps in x (scaled by 0x8014E358), y and z, the angle between them (arc_tangent_2, wrap_radians), each man's state for the shot (camera_state_bits) and target (target_slot_of), and sets the eye and target from them, with some random choice (next_random_number), kept inside the area (inside_area_bounds), eased toward (ease_toward) and set as the frame's camera (set_frame_camera). In the six-man engine the slots are tested against rw_cam_view (rw_cam_view_s5). (2026-11-13, names5: confirmed by mod/src/arena_ringstage.c ('the ring's two men go to func_800E38A4') and the lifted C++: the pair's gaps and the angle between them set the camera).
