// Writes the money back to the save image (*0x800F6134), the reverse of load_money_from_save: keeps the word at 0x80090B94 (the money) at 99,999,990 (0x05F5E0F6) or less, stores the byte 0x800A9350 at +0x6B83 and the money at +0x6B84, then calls func_80004EE8. (2026-11-12: renamed from clamp_money, which is only its first step; load_money_from_save reads the same two places.)
