// The places of line `line` in a list whose two columns start at `origins` (+0 / +2 the first column's x / y, +0x18 / +0x1A the second's): `x` gets the two x's and `y` the two y's moved down (line x 2 + 2) x 7; with `flags` 0x80 lines 0-6 go in the first column and 7-13 in the second (the other column's x set to 0), else both columns show line `line`. No callers in the recompiled code.
