// Bit bit of mask; bit 0x15 counts only when the match type (0x800A957C) has no bit 2. Caller fill_screen_14_rows (up to 0x17 entries). (2026-11-12, names4: confirmed from the lifted C++: the name says only what the code does).
// From the N64 function at 0x8013D8BC (13 instructions).
// Called by: fill_screen_14_rows.
// Random-tested: 200000 plain random inputs, all instructions reached, no difference.
s32 mask_bit_allowed(s32 mask, s32 bit) {
    s32 result;

    if (bit == 0x15) {
        result = 0;
        if (!(GAME_VAR(match_type) & 2)) {
            result = mask & (1 << (bit & 31));
        }
    } else {
        result = mask & (1 << (bit & 31));
    }
    return result;
}

// Fills screen 14's rows (0x7B00.., *0x80159484) with `count` entries (up to 0x17) through try_turn_apron_corner (func_8013D8BC); callers init_menu_screen_14 and screen_14_run. (2026-11-12, names3: confirmed from the lifted C++: entries are the indices 0-0x16 that mask_bit_allowed(0, i) (the func_8013D8BC above) allows; it skips `count` of them first, then fills the rows from *0x80159484 (six at most) and returns the count.)
